					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-3164512#post-3558056</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-3164512/autoerotic-assassination#post-3558056</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 26 Jul 2017 03:50:09 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Chubert</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>502908</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm sitting at a tentative-ish upvote. I think the thematic tangling of sex and violence (extremely common) with 173 (not so much) is super well done, especially the way you also toss in the shame and confusion. On the other hand, I felt like the progression of the story was pretty linear-that 173 is taking Lopez over is even explicitly stated-and for a story that takes place almost entirely within the mind of someone on that linear track, this kind of constrains the ways in which the story can surprise me after the first scene. Still a +1 though.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
